    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0337" n="297" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v12/pg297"/>

                <head>128. Memorandum From the Secretary of Defense (Wilson) to the Executive Secretary of the National
                    Security Council (Lay)<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d128-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-05-15"><hi rendition="#italic">May 15,
                        1956</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>U.S. Adherence to the Baghdad Pact</item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>REFERENCES</head>
                    <item>1. Memo from the JCS to the Sec Def,
                        subject as above, dated 23 March 1956<anchor n="2" xml:id="d128-f2"/></item>
                    <item>2. Memo from the Sec Def to the Executive Secretary, NSC, subject as above, dated 5 April
                            1956<anchor n="3" xml:id="d128-f3"/></item>
                    <item>3. Letter from the Sec Def to the Secretary of State, dated 6 [5] April
                            1956<anchor n="4" xml:id="d128-f4"/></item>
                    <item>4. Letter from the Secretary of State to the Sec Def, dated 23 April
                            1956<anchor n="5" xml:id="d128-f5"/></item>
                </list>
                <pb facs="0338" n="298" xml:id="pg298"/>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>This is in reference to my memorandum of 5 April 1956. I have subsequently
                        received a letter from the Secretary of State in which he advises that
                        immediate adherence by the United States to the Baghdad Pact would be
                        politically inadvisable.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>It is also my understanding that a review of NSC 5428 (U.S. Objectives and Policies with Respect to the Near
                            East)<anchor n="6" xml:id="d128-f6"/> is presently pending before the
                        National Security Council. Because of this pending review and the views of
                        the Secretary of State, and in consideration of the recommendation of the
                        Joint Chiefs of Staff that adherence to the Pact is desirable from a
                        military point of view, I recommend that the problem be considered by the
                        National Security Council sometime during the latter part of 1956 to
                        determine the desirability of announcing U.S. adherence during the January
                        1957 meeting of the Pact Council.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d128-f7"/></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">CE.
                            Wilson</hi><anchor n="8" xml:id="d128-f8"/></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
